The recurrence implementation is independently written from the equations in:
Training-Free Looped Transformers, Lizhang Chen et al., arXiv:2605.23872.
https://arxiv.org/html/2605.23872v1
No code from the paper's unavailable reference repository is included.

The build downloads and modifies a separate copy of llama.cpp:
https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp
Its original source retains its MIT license and original notices.
The local runtime adapter and patching script are AGPL-3.0-or-later.
Distributions of a combined modified runtime must preserve all applicable notices.

The build can download Khronos Vulkan-Headers and SPIRV-Headers.
Their upstream licenses and notices are retained in their checkouts.

The plugin uses @lmstudio/sdk and its dependencies under their respective licenses.
The optional Engine Protocol installer locally hard-links an already installed
official LM Studio runtime. No LM Studio binaries or proprietary source are
redistributed in this repository. Those installed components retain their terms.
This repository does not include pretrained model weights or grant rights to them.

The optional public-task benchmark uses the separately installed EleutherAI
lm-evaluation-harness and GSM8K / BIG-Bench Hard datasets. Their upstream
licenses apply. Public experiment records include the selected input questions,
reference answers and task configurations, with MIT notices retained under
reports/research-data/upstream-licenses/. Full upstream datasets and evaluation
software are linked rather than bundled. LoopLab-generated outputs, measurements
and annotations are distinguished from these inputs in the data documentation.
Original project data and figures use AGPL-3.0-or-later to the extent copyright
applies; this does not relicense upstream material or pretrained models.
